{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head dea6935fe616fc26349fd3cf2c5836774986284b, tree a94f21e1dae5ed2a790870bdb3a47f3e5b5175e0, on builder/cb3-refresh-press-20261117, all 6 artifacts, for request 0e5910f4 under my promise 1839b943. This verdict names the one implementation: CB-3 (request 6c8173e7, promise 7c5765f8, report 756d34df, the CB-3 note, primary). Main 9d585505 is the parent. This head carries out ruling 436a613f.\n\n## What I read\n\n`packages/mcp/browser/main.ts`:\n\n- The refresh timer now calls `refresh()`, which does not set `busy` and keeps its promise in `refreshing`. The promise never rejects. On an error, the read reschedules when the host answers busy, and otherwise calls `showError`. `finally` clears `refreshing` and renders. Because the promise resolves only after `finally`, a waiting press sees `refreshing` as null and the card that the read left.\n- A bound button and the title link run through `whenSettled()`. They run at once when no read is in flight, or after the read ends. Then they check `alive`, `busy` and `currentGesture`. A changed card shows CHANGED_GESTURE and sends nothing. An unchanged card runs the action.\n- `read()`, `act()` and `openDeclared()` wait for a background read, then set `busy` as before. So a read the member starts, and every act, still disable the controls.\n- The timer starts no read while `busy` or `refreshing` is set.\n- `act()` still checks the captured gesture and sends the captured cut, so a press made stale by the read cannot sign.\n\nThe test host, `views-host.ts`, adds a test-only `holdRefresh()` that holds the next `view_read` with `refresh: true`. The witness adds two cases at each width.\n\n## Answer to the planner's coverage question (6cf13658)\n\nThe builder's assert be22c6ff lists the same three controls. There is no bridge or unit case. `main.ts` runs only in the card page, and no unit test loads it. `bridge.test.ts` covers the reconciler and the bridge, which CB-3 does not change. The browser witness carries both branches, and each branch has a named red in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-cb3-gate/witness/`:\n\n- Unchanged card, the press runs. `control-b-always-changed.log`, a mutant that treats every card as changed, times out at line 207, waiting for the second chat message.\n- Changed card, nothing is sent and the notice shows. `control-c-gesture-always-current.log`, a mutant that skips the gesture check, times out at line 221, waiting for the CHANGED_GESTURE notice. That run finished at 21:30, after the review request.\n- The whole behaviour. `control-main-main-ts.log`, with main's `main.ts`, fails \"A background read leaves the card idle\" (aria-busy true).\n\nThe 3 runs on this head end without error. I accept the witness in place of a bridge case.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The gate, END d291d8f6. `gate.log` names head dea6935f and tree a94f21e1 with 0 changed files. Plain 4996 with 1 skipped and Native 1165 with 2 skipped passed. Lost crossings were 0, and the log ends \"gate passed\". The Plain count is unchanged from LW-1 because no unit test was added.\n- Scope. The 6 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 9d585505 dea6935f`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Background reads no longer lock the card. Member reads and acts keep the lock. Every press is judged against the card that is current when it runs.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A press made stale by a background read cannot act, and no new message or permission was added. `holdRefresh` lives only in the test host.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\n## For a notes-only follow-up (not blocking)\n\n1. The note names only the main control. Name controls b and c, which are the reds for each branch.\n2. The note says the notice from a waiting press \"stays\". The next background read clears it, because `refresh()` sets `notice = \"\"` at its start. On Grow that is about 2 s later. State that. CB-3 makes stale presses more likely, so the planner may want the CHANGED_GESTURE notice to survive one background read. That is a product choice, not part of this approval.\n\nThe note's limits stand: the Read points click with unknown cause, and an arrow key during a background read moving from the earlier position. That move is a read and signs nothing. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:756d34df6f104071f637cb4ac840ddd4670f27f3","binding":"assigned","head":"dea6935fe616fc26349fd3cf2c5836774986284b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1839b943b796968c40fee8c661e31f4ddb653609\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:be22c6ff61dc3702aeb49a368755ad467912a866\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c5765f828221d565dacfd74981d37579ad7ad38\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b07cea116d0f4a12862fb5ae4a1922890785471","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}